nd $f(B)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X+3.$"] [:db/cas 17592186366302 :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X+3 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X+3I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(B)={B}^{2}+B+3I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(B):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(B) & ={B}^{2}+B+3I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+2+3 & 0+1+0 \\\\ 0+(-4)+0 & 0+(-2)+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X+3 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X+3I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(B)={B}^{2}+B+3I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(B):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(B) & ={B}^{2}+B+3I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0+2+3 & 0+1+0 \\\\ 0+(-4)+0 & 0+(-2)+3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186366304 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186366305 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186366306 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186366307 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186366308 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186366309 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(H)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X+2.$" "Consider the matrix $H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(H)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X+2.$"] [:db/cas 17592186366309 :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X+2 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(H)={H}^{2}+H+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${H}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(H):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(H) & ={H}^{2}+H+2I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{align